# scripts/wallet-e2e.sh on the Mac mini (Apple M4), 2026-11-03, branch wallet-e2e.
# Prebuilt LEZ v0.4.0-rc1 sequencer_service --features standalone, fresh chain on
# 127.0.0.1:3230 (stopped at the end). Binaries built from this branch with the local risc0
# toolchain. Wall time 18.5 minutes, 15 of them the registry's commitment wait
# (MIN_COMMIT_AGE_MS), overlapped with the token and testimonial steps.
#
# Edited for size only: five "Transaction data is Public(...)" lines (the full segment
# transactions `wallet-tokens deploy` prints, 1.4 MB) are left out, as the script now does
# itself, and the "waiting Ns before revealing" lines are left in. Nothing below is secret: F
# is LEZ's published local-test account, the rest are throwaway keys on a chain that no
# longer exists.
#
# The module job's half, run the same day on the same machine:
